        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A hexagon motif table runner is 18 flat hexagons in two staggered rows, each motif 12 cm across and joined with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "join as you go",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "join-as-you-go"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " seam on the final round. The finished runner is 24 × 90 cm: long enough for a six-place table and wide enough to see. Each motif is worked from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "magic ring",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " through four rounds. Block each motif flat before joining, and block the assembled runner once more at the end."
          }
        ]
      },
